ada: weak-import pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling (absent on musl)

libgnarl's Initialize_Lock references pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling with
a strong import, so on musl -- which implements neither the function nor
PTHREAD_PRIO_PROTECT -- every statically linked tasking program dies at link
time with an undefined reference, even though the call itself is guarded by
Ceiling_Support (Locking_Policy = 'C' plus CAP_SYS_NICE, i.e. almost never
taken):

    s-taprop.adb:376: undefined reference to `pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling'

Apply the file's own established idiom for optional libc symbols (see
pthread_attr_setaffinity_np right below): mark the import Weak_External and
have Get_Ceiling_Support report False when the symbol is absent, so ceiling
locking degrades exactly like the existing no-permission case.  Ceiling
locking cannot work on musl anyway (pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol rejects
PTHREAD_PRIO_PROTECT with ENOTSUP).

Our own discovery, not in Alpine aports -- Alpine defaults gnatlink to
shared libgnat (their 0015), where the lazy reference never surfaces; the
static-first posture of this toolchain hits it immediately.  Upstream
candidate (gcc bugzilla, component ada).

--- a/gcc/ada/libgnarl/s-osinte__linux.ads
+++ b/gcc/ada/libgnarl/s-osinte__linux.ads
@@ -457,6 +457,9 @@
      (attr        : access pthread_mutexattr_t;
       prioceiling : int) return int;
    pragma Import (C, pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling);
+   pragma Weak_External (pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling);
+   --  Use a weak symbol because this function may be available or not,
+   --  depending on the C library (musl does not provide it).
 
    type struct_sched_param is record
       sched_priority : int;  --  scheduling priority
--- a/gcc/ada/libgnarl/s-taprop__linux.adb
+++ b/gcc/ada/libgnarl/s-taprop__linux.adb
@@ -224,6 +224,13 @@
          return False;
       end if;
 
+      --  Ceiling locking requires pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling; do
+      --  nothing if the C library does not provide it (e.g. musl).
+
+      if pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling'Address = Null_Address then
+         return False;
+      end if;
+
       declare
          function geteuid return Integer;
          pragma Import (C, geteuid, "geteuid");
